{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>Seed</b> — a vav before it, and also a vav in יעבדנו (\"will serve Him\"). שב אל כי לה' המלוכה (\"return, for to YHWH is the kingship\"). And the meaning: like וחסד ה' מעולם ועד עולם על יראיו (\"and the kindness of YHWH is from eternity to eternity upon those who fear Him\"). And thus: בני עבדיך ישכנו (\"the children of Your servants shall dwell\"), and the word אשר is missing, like עם לבבכם שלם (\"with your heart complete\"), as if it were זרע אשר יעבדנו (\"seed that will serve Him\"), and they are the children of the humble mentioned above." "And the meaning of לדור (\"to the generation\") — to the coming generation; therefore after it: יבואו (\"they shall come\"), in the manner of דור הולך ודור בא (\"a generation goes and a generation comes\")."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "The phrase 'שב אל כי לה' המלוכה' appears to cite I Chronicles 29:11 in connection with a textual or exegetical point; its exact function in the argument is unclear."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:21.819342562Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}